# Render and finishing

- Validate opening, representative middle, ending, and worst-case frames locally before any paid render. Use the lowest-cost tier that can reveal the defect under review.
- Finishing timelines are frame-driven and deterministic. Do not use wall-clock CSS animation, `Math.random()`, or runtime-dependent timing for titles, captions, end cards, or branding.
- Preserve source framing by default. Cross-aspect variants use a safe contain layout unless a reviewed, face-safe reframe explicitly authorizes cropping.
- Captions must share locked dialogue timing, pass reading-speed/overlap/line/safe-area checks, and remain clear of important faces and action.
- Automated finishing may assemble approved picture, audio, titles, captions, branding, and delivery variants. It may not make a failed source visually approved or relabel a preview as final.
- Prefer the existing deterministic FFmpeg/editorial contracts. Add another renderer only behind an adapter, with its license, determinism, and cost reviewed first.

